# Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth with Multiversal Passage entering after it: both are layer-4 type effects with no
# dependency between them (CR 613.8a: neither changes what the other applies to), so they apply in timestamp order
# (CR 613.7). Urborg's older effect adds Swamp, then Passage's newer "This land is the chosen type" sets its subtypes
# to Island alone (CR 305.7). Passage taps only for blue; Bot1's Plains is still a Swamp.

[Bot1 Deck]
Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth
Plains
Multiversal Passage
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Multiversal Passage.Play
Bot1.Modes(Island)
Bot1.Accept
! Bot1.Battlefield.Multiversal Passage.Activate(Ability: Add {B})
Bot1.Battlefield.Multiversal Passage.Activate

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Mana = {U}
Bot1.Battlefield.Multiversal Passage.Subtypes = Island
Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Subtypes = Swamp
